#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:15
msgid "Using Improved Dynamic Discovery - tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:18
msgid ""
"ROS nodes can automatically discover each other, but some systems need more "
"control over discovery range and peer selection. This article shows how to "
"configure improved dynamic discovery with ``ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE`` "
"and ``ROS_STATIC_PEERS``. After you follow these steps, you can limit "
"discovery to localhost, the subnet, or specific remote peers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:26
msgid ""
"**Goal:** This tutorial will show how to use the improved dynamic discovery "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:28
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Advanced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:30
msgid "**Time:** 15 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:34
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:37
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:39
msgid ""
"By default, ROS 2 will attempt to find all nodes on all hosts on the same "
"subnet automatically. However, the following options are available to "
"control the ROS 2 discovery range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:44
msgid ""
"These environment variables (``ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE`` and "
"``ROS_STATIC_PEERS``) are **not supported** by ``rmw_zenoh``. If you are "
"using ``rmw_zenoh`` as your RMW implementation, please refer to the "
"`rmw_zenoh configuration documentation <https://github.com/ros2/rmw_zenoh?"
"tab=readme-ov-file#configuration>`_ for instructions on how to configure "
"discovery and communication behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:49
msgid "Configuration Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:51
msgid ""
"``ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE``: controls how far ROS nodes will try to "
"discover each other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:53
msgid "Valid options are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:55
msgid ""
"``SUBNET`` is the default, and for DDS based middleware it means it will "
"discover any node reachable via multicast."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:56
msgid ""
"``LOCALHOST`` means a node will only try to discover other nodes on the same "
"machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:57
msgid ""
"``OFF`` means the node won't discover any other nodes, even on the same "
"machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:58
msgid "``SYSTEM_DEFAULT`` means \"don't change any discovery settings\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:60
msgid ""
"``ROS_STATIC_PEERS``: is a semicolon (``;``) separated list of addresses "
"that ROS should try to discover nodes on. This allows connecting to nodes on "
"specific machines (as long as their discovery range is not set to ``OFF``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:63
msgid ""
"The combination of these two environment variables for local and remote "
"nodes will enable and control the ROS 2 communication discovery range. The "
"following tables highlight the discovery range behavior for possible "
"combination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Improved-Dynamic-Discovery.rst:66
msgid ""
"A ``X`` indicates that nodes A and B will not discover each other and "
"communicate. A ``O`` indicates that nodes A and B will discover each other "
"and communicate."
msgstr ""

